  "notes": "The rock-and-funk-facing edge of the lane, and the entry says the kit is \"closer to a rock/funk kit than to the behind-the-beat soul kit\": \"live kit played hard and dry — kick on 1 and the offbeat of 2, snare cracked on 2&4, open hats and crashes used as accents rather than as a carpet, and handclaps doubling the backbeat\". So `secondaryAnchor` is 2&, the velocity tiers are the hardest in this batch, the hat is deliberately non-continuous at a fill density of 0.22 while `openHat.prob` runs at 0.42, and the percussion lanes are snaps and crashes rather than congas. The band is the entry's 84–118 with \"a genuine rock-tempo subset above 110\". Harmony is the stated \"short vamps rather than cycles, and a habit of holding one dominant chord for a whole verse\", which is `maxChords` 2, chord durations of 8–16 beats and a mixolydian/lydian scale set for the \"blues sevenths and Lydian colour\". Melody is \"high-tenor into falsetto, riff-shaped (it doubles the guitar figure), and low in melisma\", so the structure is a riff loop with a high chord-tone bias and a wide interval spread, and the counter echoes it at the octave. Bass is \"distorted or compressed, syncopated 16ths, mixed at guitar level\". ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all drum probabilities and velocity tiers and every melody number; the research marks the tempo/drum detail as inference and [LOW-CONF].",
